# Forms & Validation — React Hook Form + Zod

## When to use

- **≥2 fields:** React Hook Form + Zod — no raw `useState` per field
- **Single confirm/input:** simple controlled input or dialog is acceptable

## Schema-first

Zod schema in `features/<module>/core/schema.ts` is the single source of truth:

```ts
import { z } from 'zod';
import { zodResolver } from '@hookform/resolvers/zod';

export const employeeSchema = z.object({ ... });
export type EmployeeFormValues = z.infer<typeof employeeSchema>;

// In form component:
const form = useForm<EmployeeFormValues>({
  resolver: zodResolver(employeeSchema),
  defaultValues: { ... },
});
```

- Infer types with `z.infer<typeof schema>` — do not duplicate interfaces
- Reuse shared validators from `lib/validation/` (`emailSchema`, `phoneVnSchema`, `codeFieldSchema`)
- Validation messages via `txt('module.validation.key')` from `lib/text`

## Form UI

- Use `RhfDataField` / form primitives from `@/components/views` when available
- Layout: `FormGrid`, `FormSection` / `Section` with `variant="primary"` (see `06-project-5f.mdc`)
- Required fields: pass `required={true}` on `Input` / `Textarea` for asterisk display (validation still from Zod)
- Error messages: `text-xs` under fields (built into Input/Select/Textarea components)

## Drawer forms

- Width: `DRAWER_WIDTH_FORM` or `getDrawerWidthClass(stackLevel)` from `lib/dialog-sizes.ts`
- Stacked drawer (form opened from detail): `stackLevel={1}` on `GenericDrawer`
- Submit via `handleSubmit`; disable submit while `isSubmitting`

## Edit vs create

- Same schema; use `defaultValues` from entity for edit mode
- Reset form when drawer opens with new entity: `form.reset(values)` in effect keyed on `open` + `entityId`

## Do not

- Use Formik, Yup, or uncontrolled forms without RHF in feature modules
- Put Zod schema inline in component files — keep in `core/schema.ts`
- Skip server-side validation assumptions — client Zod is UX; Supabase RLS + DB constraints are authoritative
